[1marray-bag[0m  [2mphp/value-objects[0m
  [2malso answers to ArrayBagDetector, ArrayBag, csharp-dictionary-bag, DictionaryBagDetector, DictionaryBag, python-dict-bag, DictBagDetector, DictBag[0m
  String-indexing (`$arr['key']`) a structured array param instead of giving it a name —
  the type was never defined.

[33mWhy it is a sin[0m

  Data that travels together is a **thing**, not a loose pile of arrays and primitives.
  The moment a
  cluster of values is passed around, returned, or reached into by string keys, it wants a
  name and a type.

[33mHow to fix it[0m

  Give a structured array a typed value object — never read a named field by string key
  off an `array` param.
  A Spatie `Data` object built via `::from($array)`.

[33mCommands[0m

  [36mLearn     [0m load the skill [1mcommandments-php-value-objects[0m
  [36mFind it   [0m commandments judge --sin=array-bag
  [36mTurn off  [0m commandments disable array-bag
  [36mWrong?    [0m commandments report --detector=array-bag --reason="…" --ref=PATH:LINE


[1marray-return-bag[0m  [2mphp/value-objects[0m
  [2malso answers to ArrayReturnBagDetector, ArrayReturnBag, csharp-array-return-bag, python-dict-return-bag, DictReturnBagDetector, DictReturnBag[0m
  Returning a multi-field string-keyed array literal (a bag that should be a value object)

[33mWhy it is a sin[0m

  Data that travels together is a **thing**, not a loose pile of arrays and primitives.
  The moment a
  cluster of values is passed around, returned, or reached into by string keys, it wants a
  name and a type.

[33mHow to fix it[0m

  Return a typed value object, not a multi-field string-keyed array literal.
  Return a Spatie `Data` object via `::from(...)`.

